        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-03T23:26:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It exits unsuccessfully after printing a message about the opendir() call failing. What\u0027s happening here is that kati walks the entire tree at startup creating an in memory representation of the filesystem. That way, later when we would execute a find call, we can do it entirely in memory instead of asking the filesystem. When we do a lot of find calls, that adds up. But it\u0027s apparently not very safe to remove a directory when that scan is happening.",
      "parentUuid": "29182647_e9f5f6ed",
      "revId": "c6f7842be43136b30b359b51ebd075bc2d5fffa8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
